      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "AMYS BABY ANGEL (3) could only manage to finish sixth at her latest appearance over 2050m at Port Pirie, a poor reflection on her short quote. Form prior to that was far better, including a very close fourth over 1800m at this track two starts ago. Will enjoy a nice run from this favourable starting position. This doesn't look as hard so she is a major player. MALACHITE ROCK (8) has been competitive of late and kept the ball rolling last time when 4 metres from the winner in third over 1800m at this track. Can settle just behind them and wait on the sprint lane. Won't find this any harder and he can take care of this line-up. FLYIN TOMMY NZ (9) is worth another chance after a last-start seventh over 1800m at this track four weeks ago. CROOKWELL JAKE (6) is in the mix at his first run since finishing fourth over 2230m at this track six months ago.",
